OneiOS take18, userland/metal/patches/NativeMetal/0008: MTLFunction.functionConstantsDictionary, one dictionary per
unspecialized function of a library.
Upstream: Droid-VM/NativeMetal 36514d3 (2026-11-13) and 438a7c5 (2026-11-15), both wip/hackintosh, lateautumn233, in one
patch: 36514d3 alone would rebuild the dictionary from the runtime's reflection JSON at every call (VFX asks for fresh
function objects every frame), which 438a7c5 then caches. 438a7c5 keys its cache on 8c1ea13's NBFunction.sourceName,
which b0d6a07 has not: here it keys on NBFunction.name, the name the function was looked up by in its library (b0d6a07
keeps no aliases, so the two are the same name). Otherwise verbatim (README hunks left out).
What: NBFunction answers functionConstantsDictionary with an NBFunctionConstant (name, type, index, required) per
function constant of the runtime's reflection (nmb_function_constants, new in NativeMetalObjects.h/.rs, over the
runtime's Function::function_constants_dictionary). A specialized function (made with constant values, the zero-rest
rebuilds of 0007 included) answers an empty dictionary; an unspecialized one of a library shares its library's entry; a
function made with no library (shader priming's zero-constant variants) builds its own.
Why: correctness. b0d6a07 answered nil through its missing-selector fallback: a client that reads the constants to fill
MTLFunctionConstantValues (VFX, Swift code) set none, and its specialized functions were refused or wrong.
Switch: none (correctness fix). Removable: yes (ONEIOS_METAL_SKIP=function-constants-dictionary); 0010 is left out with it.

